$ Milestone 7, §5.4/§7/§9: `environment.*`. `has` is already a reserved
$ Fly keyword (§15.6), so the exists-check is spelled `exists`, not
$ `has`. An unset variable returns EMP from `get` rather than throwing.

bring environment

show(environment.exists("FLY_TEST_DEFINITELY_UNSET_XYZ"))
show(environment.get("FLY_TEST_DEFINITELY_UNSET_XYZ"))

environment.set("FLY_TEST_VAR", "hello from fly")
show(environment.exists("FLY_TEST_VAR"))
show(environment.get("FLY_TEST_VAR"))

environment.set("FLY_TEST_VAR", "overwritten")
show(environment.get("FLY_TEST_VAR"))
